/T (Function: `init_db\(\)` This function is strictly responsible for schema validation and creation. Upon startup, it establishes a synchronous connection to the local database file and executes a `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` Data Definition Language \(DDL\) statement. This preemptive check ensures that the application never attempts to insert data into a non-existent table during the multithreaded loop, an error which would trigger a fatal `sqlite3.OperationalError` and cause an immediate system shutdown.)
/E (Function: `init_db\(\)` This function is strictly responsible for schema validation and creation. Upon startup, it establishes a synchronous connection to the local database file and executes a `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` Data Definition Language \(DDL\) statement. This preemptive check ensures that the application never attempts to insert data into a non-existent table during the multithreaded loop, an error which would trigger a fatal `sqlite3.OperationalError` and cause an immediate system shutdown.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
226 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 106 0 R
/T (Function: `monitor_and_heal\(target_app\)` This algorithm handles the core Service Reliability Engineering logic. It utilizes the `psutil` library to scan active hardware threads. Instead of allocating significant memory for a massive, static array of all active processes, the algorithm utilizes a highly optimized Python generator expression: `if target_app not in \(p.name\(\).lower\(\) for p in psutil.process_iter\(['name']\)\):`. If the target string is absent, it immediately executes `subprocess.Popen\(target_app\)` to force a localized application reboot. This is the cornerstone of the self-healing infrastructure.)
/E (Function: `monitor_and_heal\(target_app\)` This algorithm handles the core Service Reliability Engineering logic. It utilizes the `psutil` library to scan active hardware threads. Instead of allocating significant memory for a massive, static array of all active processes, the algorithm utilizes a highly optimized Python generator expression: `if target_app not in \(p.name\(\).lower\(\) for p in psutil.process_iter\(['name']\)\):`. If the target string is absent, it immediately executes `subprocess.Popen\(target_app\)` to force a localized application reboot. This is the cornerstone of the self-healing infrastructure.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
