233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (The schema relies entirely on Python's native `sqlite3` library, requiring no external drivers or ORMs. The primary DDL statement executed upon boot explicitly defines the structure of the transactional ledger. It establishes a `transactions` table encompassing a highly specific set of columns designed to mirror retail data.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (5.2 SQL Execution Patterns)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (To maximize query execution speed and minimize dependency weight, the script completely circumvents heavy Object-Relational Mappers \(ORMs\) like SQLAlchemy. Database cursors are aggressively instantiated, executed, committed, and closed \(`conn.close\(\)`\) entirely within a singular function scope during every single loop iteration.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (The schema demands a `txn_id` structured as a `TEXT PRIMARY KEY` to ensure absolute uniqueness. Transaction variables are synthesized using core libraries, with the `txn_id` generated using programmatic f-string concatenation: `f"TXN- {random.randint\(1000, 9999\)}"`. The floating-point mathematics for item pricing and totals are explicitly bounded in Python using `round\(value, 2\)` prior to insertion, completely eliminating floating-point arithmetic pollution within the SQLite `REAL` columns. This strict database modeling prevents historical drift.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (The parameterization tuple is strictly enforced during execution: `c.execute\("INSERT INTO transactions VALUES \(?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?\)", \(client_id, name, quantity, avg_price, total, timestamp\)\)`. This specific scoping and rigid parameterization strategy actively prevents SQL injection attacks and absolutely negates the "Database is Locked" exceptions that consistently plague persistent, multi-threaded SQLite connections in high-throughput environments. It is a critical layer of defensive programming.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
