/P 110 0 R
/E (Because the AI Self-Healing Cloud is designed to run indefinitely on edge hardware, strict memory optimization is enforced at both the Python backend and the JavaScript frontend.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (On the presentation layer, the low-level rendering strategy focuses on strict JavaScript array manipulation to actively restrict browser RAM consumption over extended operational lifecycles. The Chart.js implementation natively pushes the `latest_total` payload directly into an active coordinate array each time a WebSocket payload is received, explicitly avoiding total page refresh states which would spike CPU usage.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (To ensure the browser tab does not suffer memory exhaustion or critical DOM rendering lag if the kiosk runs unattended for multiple days, an algorithmic garbage collection check is implemented within the `socket.on` listener block. Once the `data.labels.length` property exceeds a hardcoded limit of 15 indices, the script automatically triggers the JavaScript `.shift\(\)` array method. This aggressively and permanently discards the oldest data point from active client memory before rendering the new graphical frame. This creates a lightweight sliding window effect that completely eliminates client-side memory bloat.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
