/P 111 0 R
/E (The application is heavily fortified at the runtime execution level to prevent hostile intrusion, unauthorized data access, and unsafe code execution, which is critical for software operating in a physical retail environment.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 111 0 R
/E (The Flask server initialization call is permanently hardcoded to `app.run\(debug=False\)`. This explicitly and irrevocably disables the Werkzeug interactive debugger. This is a paramount security mandate; leaving the debugger active would allow any user with access to the browser console to execute arbitrary Python code directly against the host OS \(Remote Code Execution\), compromising the entire kiosk.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 111 0 R
/E (Furthermore, thread synchronization issues related to the Python Global Interpreter Lock \(GIL\) are natively resolved by assigning `async_mode='threading'` to the SocketIO configuration parameters. This ensures that the web server explicitly respects standard Python library parallelism rather than attempting unsafe asynchronous context switching \(like Eventlet or Gevent\) across the strict database cursor boundaries, which could lead to data corruption.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
