758 0 obj
<<
/Title (Function: `init_db\(\)` This function is strictly responsible for schema validation and creation. Upon startup, it establishes a synchronous connection to the local database file and executes a `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` Data Definition Language \(DDL\) statement. This preemptive check ensures that the application never attempts to insert data into a non-existent table during the multithreaded loop, an error which would trigger a fatal `sqlite3.OperationalError` and cause an immediate system shutdown.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 760 0 R
/Next 756 0 R
>>
endobj
